From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:35:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0007: kernel service requests are not lost

The kernel service thread cleared its request count after
io_context.run() returned: a request made in between - a timer scheduled
as run() ran out of work - was wiped out, the thread slept again with
that timer pending, and a game waiting for it waited forever (FIFA 22
and FC 27 at boot, one launch out of two). Requests are now taken before
running. Upstream defect, still on main on 2026-10-27.

Details: tools/shadps4/README.md in the GameFlex repository, entry 0007.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/core/libraries/kernel/kernel.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/libraries/kernel/kernel.cpp b/src/core/libraries/kernel/kernel.cpp
index 1bd11811..f8d8d1ff 100644
--- a/src/core/libraries/kernel/kernel.cpp
+++ b/src/core/libraries/kernel/kernel.cpp
@@ -68,6 +68,11 @@ static void KernelServiceThread(std::stop_token stoken) {
         {
             std::unique_lock lock{m_asio_req};
             Common::CondvarWait(cv_asio_req, lock, stoken, [] { return asio_requests != 0; });
+            // GameFlex: the requests are taken BEFORE running. Reset after run() returned, a
+            // request made in between — a timer scheduled as run() ran out of work — was wiped
+            // out: this thread slept again with that timer pending, and a game waiting for it
+            // waited forever (EA's FIFA 22 and FC 27 at boot, one launch out of two).
+            asio_requests = 0;
         }
         if (stoken.stop_requested()) {
             break;
@@ -75,8 +80,6 @@ static void KernelServiceThread(std::stop_token stoken) {
 
         io_context.run();
         io_context.restart();
-
-        asio_requests = 0;
     }
 }
 
